<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Mithridatic War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">83–81 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mithridatic-wars">Mithridatic Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Mithridatic War (83–81 BCE) was a short conflict between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mithridates-vi-of-pontus">Mithridates VI of Pontus</a>. It began when Lucius <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/licinius">Licinius</a> Murena, the Roman governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>, invaded Pontus on his own initiative. Mithridates defeated Murena on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kizilirmak">Halys</a> river in 82 BCE, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulla">Sulla</a> ordered an end to the fighting, restoring the terms of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-dardanos">Treaty of Dardanos</a>.</p></div>
